      "writtenOn": "2022-03-25T17:08:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Couldn\u0027t the inliner cause this to occur? I don\u0027t think we change the position of an inlined element (and don\u0027t think we need to). e.g.\n\n  void foo(int a, int b) {\n      return b / a;\n  }\n  void bar() { return foo(0, 1); }\n  \nI think we may end up inside the Constant Folder with something that looks like\n\n  return 1 / 0;\n         ^^^^^   divide by zero\n\nWhere the 0 and 1 have flipped positions. Up until this point it\u0027s been a non-concern.",
      "parentUuid": "bc20d555_fc31b13a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 67,
        "endChar": 59
      },
